# Bleeding your prey: a block that leads to combat, then a bleed that gets through.
# Cards are given by VEKN ID; names and images come from the content pack (LEGAL-08).
seed 3
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
seat D dave
crypt A 200107 *3 200848 *3 200734 *3 200106 *3
library A 101055 *10 100845 *8 100401 *8 100199 *6 100598 *4 100518 *4
crypt B 200534 *4 200842 *4 200117 *4
library B 100573 *10 100518 *10 100401 *10 100199 *10
crypt C 200378 *6 200107 *6
library C 100001 *10 101321 *10 100845 *10 100984 *10
crypt D 200106 *6 200848 *6
library D 100598 *10 102137 *10 101743 *10 100059 *10
start

# Fast-forward: everyone has brought out a vampire or two (sped up for the demo).
A> transfer +7 A:uncontrolled:3
A> move A:uncontrolled:3 ready
A> transfer +8 A:uncontrolled:3
A> move A:uncontrolled:3 ready
B> transfer +8 B:uncontrolled:2
B> move B:uncontrolled:2 ready
C> transfer +5 C:uncontrolled:1
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready
D> transfer +10 D:uncontrolled:1
D> move D:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# Alice bleeds her prey, Bob. Only Bob may block, and he does: combat.
A> bleed A:ready:1
expect action bleed A blocks
expect impulse B
B> block B:ready:1
A> pass
B> pass
expect action bleed A combat
B> endcombat
expect action none

# Her second vampire bleeds Bob too, adding a modifier. Bob doesn't block.
A> bleed A:ready:2
B> pass
expect action bleed A resolution
A> play A:hand:1
A> resolve success 2 edge
expect pool B 20
expect edge A
